---
# The bounds (MAX_MSGS, MAX_ADOPTS, one Q) end every behaviour with both
# children at rest: that is the end of the flow, not a deadlock.
deadlock_detection: false
---

# Stopping background agents, as the parent's Work dialog and serve see
# it: the Stop button's state machine (Stopping, Retry, No reply), Stop
# on a queued agent, and a child whose turn closed with calls adopted as
# jobs (it is still working: "waiting"), then woken when they finish.
#
# Code: go/internal/serve/web/src/work-ui.tsx (useStopStore,
# StopWorkButton), work.ts (agentsFromRows: row life and canStop),
# app.tsx (agentReports: the Result a row shows), children_api.go
# (stopAgent), children.go (childEventLocked, report, stopChild,
# drainQueue), supervisor.go (Send, Interrupt), and the engine's
# closeTurn/adopt/wake (internal/unreal/session/actor.go).
#
# background_agents covers the spawn budget, the queue and depth; this
# flow is what it leaves out: jobs, and the page's own stop entries.
#
# Two children. A (fields a*) carries the whole stop and job story; Q
# (q*) is spawned while A holds the only slot (running cap 1), so it
# queues, and is then stopped while queued, or drained and run.
#
# Bounds: A adopts a job at most once and is messaged at most once,
# enough for every ordering of "job still running" against "turn open".
#
# Folded into one step (nothing a client can hold them on):
#   - a Stop that reaches serve (StopLands) with a slot held: SIGINT, the
#     turn (or the idle wait) ends, the process exits and its jobs die,
#     the report lands, the page's next read clears the entry, and the
#     freed slot drains the queue;
#   - a close's report, and the freed slot's drain;
#   - a job that finishes while a turn is open is steered into it as a
#     [notice]; one that finishes while idle opens a wake turn.
# Held on purpose by a test (page.route in the browser, the adapter's own
# bookkeeping in Go): the POST /stop, so "Stopping" and its 15 s timer
# are states, and so the POST can fail (Retry).
#
# Where the code disagrees, this spec says what the flow promises and the
# code is the finding (checked against the code on main, 2026-09-24):
#   1. A waiting child (done with running>0) holds its slot in serve
#      (childEventLocked returns early) but its row reads "finished"
#      (StatusOf says done; agentsFromRows has canStop false): the Work
#      dialog shows no Stop for an agent serve counts as running.
#      Promise: RowShowsSlot.
#   2. A message to a waiting child opens a turn whose done (running=0,
#      only its own calls count) frees the slot while the old job still
#      runs; drain may start Q; the job's wake turn then runs with no
#      slot, the row says running with Stop, and Stop answers "idle"
#      without interrupting: "Stopping" until the wake closes by itself
#      or 15 s pass and it says "No reply". Promise: SlotIsWork and
#      StoppingHasRequest.
#   3. Stop on a waiting child SIGINTs an idle process: it exits, its
#      jobs die, and the exit's report finds the interim done closed and
#      tells the parent "finished" with the interim reply. Promise: the
#      notice says stopped (StopSaysStopped).
#   4. useStopStore never clears an "error" entry (the filter skips it),
#      and a POST that fails after the record already cleared the entry
#      writes a fresh "error": a finished agent keeps a Retry button.
#      Promise: StopEntryNeedsWorker.
#   5. A stopped queued agent vanishes from byKey, so its entry is never
#      cleared and flips to "timeout" 15 s later. No row renders it, so
#      it is invisible (a leak, not a wrong screen); modelled as cleared.
#   6. A row keeps the parent's last report as its Result while a new
#      turn runs (a re-messaged or woken child shows the old reply under
#      "Result"). Promise: ShownReportIsCurrent.
#
# Fields:
#   a          A's last turn as its history says: none | open | done | stopped
#   a_job      A has an adopted call still running
#   a_slot     A is in serve's running map (agentCounts' running)
#   a_row      A's Work row: none | running | finished | stopped
#   a_stop     A's stop entry: "" | stopping | error | timeout
#   a_req      a POST /stop for A is in flight
#   a_turns    turns A opened (spawn, message, wake)
#   a_shown    the turn whose report A's row shows as Result, 0 for none
#   a_notices  reports the parent got for A; a_finals the ones it is owed
#   a_word     the last report's word: "" | finished | stopped
#   a_msgs, a_adopts   bounds
#   q          none | queued | running | done | stopped | gone (dropped)
#   q_stop, q_req      Q's stop entry and request, as A's

MAX_MSGS = 1
MAX_ADOPTS = 1

role Parent:
    action Init:
        self.a = "none"
        self.a_job = False
        self.a_slot = False
        self.a_row = "none"
        self.a_stop = ""
        self.a_req = False
        self.a_turns = 0
        self.a_shown = 0
        self.a_notices = 0
        self.a_finals = 0
        self.a_word = ""
        self.a_msgs = 0
        self.a_adopts = 0
        self.q = "none"
        self.q_stop = ""
        self.q_req = False

    # agent: tools.spawn({background}) with a free slot: A runs.
    atomic action SpawnA:
        require self.a == "none"
        self.a = "open"
        self.a_slot = True
        self.a_row = "running"
        self.a_turns = 1

    # A second spawn while A holds the only slot: Q queues.
    atomic action SpawnQ:
        require self.q == "none" and self.a_slot
        self.q = "queued"

    # A's turn closes with no call of its own still running (done,
    # running=0). The parent is told; A keeps its slot while an older
    # adopted job still runs; otherwise the slot frees and the queue
    # drains into it, and the row's stop entry is over.
    atomic fair action FinishA:
        require self.a == "open"
        self.a = "done"
        self.a_finals += 1
        self.a_notices += 1
        self.a_word = "finished"
        self.a_shown = self.a_turns
        if not self.a_job:
            self.a_slot = False
            self.a_row = "finished"
            self.a_stop = ""
            if self.q == "queued":
                self.q = "running"

    # The turn settles with a call still running: the call becomes a job
    # and the turn closes (done, running=1). An interim close: no report,
    # the slot stays, the row stays running.
    atomic action AdoptA:
        require self.a == "open" and not self.a_job and self.a_adopts < MAX_ADOPTS
        self.a = "done"
        self.a_job = True
        self.a_adopts += 1

    # The adopted job finishes: inside an open turn it is a [notice];
    # with no turn open it wakes A into a turn of its own.
    atomic fair action JobEnds:
        require self.a_job
        self.a_job = False
        if self.a != "open":
            self.a = "open"
            self.a_turns += 1
            self.a_shown = 0

    # The parent (tools.message) or a person sends A another prompt; a
    # stopped A is respawned. The new turn holds a slot (Send does not
    # wait for one).
    atomic action MessageA:
        require self.a in ("done", "stopped") and self.a_msgs < MAX_MSGS
        self.a = "open"
        self.a_turns += 1
        self.a_shown = 0
        self.a_slot = True
        self.a_row = "running"
        self.a_msgs += 1

    # user: Stop on A's running row: "Stopping", the 15 s timer, POST.
    atomic action ClickStopA:
        require self.a_row == "running" and self.a_stop == ""
        self.a_stop = "stopping"
        self.a_req = True

    # user: Retry after a failed stop.
    atomic action RetryA:
        require self.a_stop == "error" and self.a_row == "running" and not self.a_req
        self.a_stop = "stopping"
        self.a_req = True

    # The POST is answered. "running": serve holds A's slot and SIGINTs
    # it (open turn or idle wait alike); the turn ends cancelled, the
    # process exits, its job dies, the parent is told "stopped" and the
    # queue drains. "idle": A holds no slot, so it is not working and its
    # row already left running; the entry is already gone.
    atomic fair action StopLandsA:
        require self.a_req
        self.a_req = False
        if self.a_slot:
            self.a = "stopped"
            self.a_job = False
            self.a_slot = False
            self.a_row = "stopped"
            self.a_stop = ""
            self.a_finals += 1
            self.a_notices += 1
            self.a_word = "stopped"
            self.a_shown = self.a_turns
            if self.q == "queued":
                self.q = "running"

    # The POST fails: "Retry", while there is still something to stop.
    atomic action StopFailsA:
        require self.a_req
        self.a_req = False
        if self.a_stop != "":
            self.a_stop = "error"

    # 15 s with the request unanswered: "No reply", until the record ends it.
    atomic fair action TimeoutA:
        require self.a_stop == "stopping"
        self.a_stop = "timeout"

    atomic action ClickStopQ:
        require self.q in ("queued", "running") and self.q_stop == ""
        self.q_stop = "stopping"
        self.q_req = True

    atomic action RetryQ:
        require self.q_stop == "error" and self.q in ("queued", "running") and not self.q_req
        self.q_stop = "stopping"
        self.q_req = True

    # "queued": dropped from the queue and meta, the row goes and so does
    # its entry. "running" (drained since the click): interrupted.
    # Anything else: already ended, nothing to do.
    atomic fair action StopLandsQ:
        require self.q_req
        self.q_req = False
        if self.q == "queued":
            self.q = "gone"
            self.q_stop = ""
        elif self.q == "running":
            self.q = "stopped"
            self.q_stop = ""

    atomic action StopFailsQ:
        require self.q_req
        self.q_req = False
        if self.q_stop != "":
            self.q_stop = "error"

    atomic fair action TimeoutQ:
        require self.q_stop == "stopping"
        self.q_stop = "timeout"

    # Q's one turn closes by itself.
    atomic fair action FinishQ:
        require self.q == "running"
        self.q = "done"
        self.q_stop = ""

action Init:
    parent = Parent()

# A holds a running slot exactly while it works: a turn open, or a job
# adopted from a closed one. So a waiting child holds one slot, a woken
# or re-messaged one still holds it, and Stop reaches it.
always assertion SlotIsWork:
    return parent.a_slot == (parent.a == "open" or parent.a_job)

# The Work row says running (and offers Stop) exactly while serve counts
# A running.
always assertion RowShowsSlot:
    return (parent.a_row == "running") == parent.a_slot

# A stop entry lives only while its worker is still running or queued:
# the record ending it clears Stopping, No reply and Retry alike.
always assertion StopEntryNeedsWorker:
    a_ok = parent.a_stop == "" or parent.a_row == "running"
    q_ok = parent.q_stop == "" or parent.q in ("queued", "running")
    return a_ok and q_ok

# "Stopping" means a request is on its way: an answer of "idle" never
# leaves a row spinning.
always assertion StoppingHasRequest:
    return (parent.a_stop != "stopping" or parent.a_req) and (parent.q_stop != "stopping" or parent.q_req)

# Every close A is owed a report for is reported once; an interim close
# (running>0) is not one of them.
always assertion ReportedOnce:
    return parent.a_notices == parent.a_finals and parent.a_finals <= parent.a_turns

# Once A has stopped working, the last report says how: stopped when the
# stop ended it, even when it was only waiting on a job.
always assertion StopSaysStopped:
    if parent.a == "open" or parent.a_job or parent.a_notices == 0:
        return True
    return (parent.a_word == "stopped") == (parent.a == "stopped")

# The Result on A's row is the report of its latest turn, never an
# earlier one while a newer turn runs or waits.
always assertion ShownReportIsCurrent:
    return parent.a_shown == 0 or (parent.a_shown == parent.a_turns and parent.a != "open")

# Every stop entry leaves "Stopping" (an answer, or the 15 s timer).
always eventually assertion StoppingEnds:
    return parent.a_stop != "stopping" and parent.q_stop != "stopping"

# A child waiting on its jobs is eventually woken and done with them.
always eventually assertion WaitingEnds:
    return not parent.a_job

# The queued child does not wait forever.
always eventually assertion QueueDrains:
    return parent.q != "queued"
